	<tr><td style="padding: 1px 1px 0 1px;">
		<a name="msg10300"></a>
		<table cellpadding="3" cellspacing="0" border="0" width="100%">
			<tr><td class="windowbg2">
				<table width="100%" cellpadding="5" cellspacing="0">
					<tr>
						<td valign="top" width="15%" rowspan="2">
							<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?action=profile;u=402" title="View the profile of Callon">Callon</a></b><br />
							<span class="smalltext">
								Drolvarg Guardian<br />
								<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/star.gif" alt="*" border="0" /><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/star.gif" alt="*" border="0" /><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/star.gif" alt="*" border="0" /><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/star.gif" alt="*" border="0" /><br />
								Posts: 320<br />
								<br />
								<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/YaBBImages/avatars/opus.gif" alt="" border="0" /><br />
								Warpig<br />
								<br />
								
								
								
								<br />
								<a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?action=profile;u=402"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/icons/profile_sm.gif" alt="View Profile" title="View Profile" border="0" /></a>
								<a href="mailto:murgen21@yahoo.com"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/email_sm.gif" alt="Email" title="Email" border="0" /></a>
							</span>
						</td>
						<td valign="top" width="85%" height="100%">
							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
								<td align="left" valign="middle"><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=1016.msg10300#msg10300"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/post/xx.gif" alt="" border="0" /></a></td>
								<td align="left" valign="middle">
									<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=1016.msg10300#msg10300">Re: Future of EQ</a></b><br />
									<span class="smalltext">&#171; <b>Reply #31 on:</b> August 20, 2004, 06:45:15 pm &#187;</span></td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" height="20" nowrap="nowrap" style="font-size: smaller;">
								</td>
							</tr></table>
							<hr width="100%" size="1" class="hrcolor" />
							<div class="quoteheader">Quote</div><div class="quote">I figure with Level 70 cap, the challenge for older content will shift from a large raid to a small raid,</div><br />But it won&#039;t shift the raid size.&nbsp; It&#039;s not like our guild is going to suddenly become a small guild.&nbsp; There&#039;s nothing forcing you to use a smaller raid on that old content.&nbsp; It will simply mean less and be easier to beat it because we&#039;ll start throwing L70s at it.<br /><br />Speaking of the future, is there even a release date for OoW yet?&nbsp; All I can find is &quot;September&quot;.<br />
						</td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<td valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
								<td align="left" colspan="2" class="smalltext">
								</td>
							</tr><tr>
								<td align="left" valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
								</td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
									<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/ip.gif" alt="" border="0" /> Logged
								</td>
							</tr></table>
						</td>
					</tr>
				</table>
			</td></tr>
		</table>
	</td></tr>
	<tr><td style="padding: 1px 1px 0 1px;">
		<a name="msg10482"></a>
		<table cellpadding="3" cellspacing="0" border="0" width="100%">
			<tr><td class="windowbg">
				<table width="100%" cellpadding="5" cellspacing="0">
					<tr>
						<td valign="top" width="15%" rowspan="2">
							<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?action=profile;u=806" title="View the profile of Khaevil">Khaevil</a></b><br />
							<span class="smalltext">
								Orc Pawn<br />
								<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/star.gif" alt="*" border="0" /><br />
								Posts: 1<br />
								<br />
								<br />
								
								
								
								<br />
								<a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?action=profile;u=806"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/icons/profile_sm.gif" alt="View Profile" title="View Profile" border="0" /></a>
							</span>
						</td>
						<td valign="top" width="85%" height="100%">
							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
								<td align="left" valign="middle"><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=1016.msg10482#msg10482"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/post/xx.gif" alt="" border="0" /></a></td>
								<td align="left" valign="middle">
									<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=1016.msg10482#msg10482">Re: Future of EQ</a></b><br />
									<span class="smalltext">&#171; <b>Reply #32 on:</b> August 26, 2004, 12:59:38 pm &#187;</span></td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" height="20" nowrap="nowrap" style="font-size: smaller;">
								</td>
							</tr></table>
							<hr width="100%" size="1" class="hrcolor" />
							As someone who&#039;s quit two MMORPGs now I&#039;ll tell ya what seems to me to be the thing that actually causes people to quit.  It&#039;s not new games comming out, it&#039;s when the game stops being fun.<br /><br />I quit EverQuest shortly after Planes of Power was released.  The new level cap and new alt abilities, now I had to grind all over again.  Items with over 127 to a stat which I thought would be the hard cap (since that&#039;s the limit for a single byte when allowing negative numbers) ment that all I had worked for up to that point would mean nothing in a couple months.  Mostly the game was no longer exciting, when grinding I was literally falling asleep at the computer in the middle of the afternoon.  I had been having fun not being uber with a small guild doing old-content raids, but with Planes of Power they all left to go be uber.  So there was nothing left in the game that was actually fun anymore, which is the reason I play games in the first place.  I suspect some people play to try to compensate for real life short commings.<br /><br />I switched to Dark Age of Camelot, which had been out for a year at the time.  I will have to say that after playing DAOC I will never play another game that focuses on PvE instead of PvP.  I look back at EQ and I know I had fun when I was playing it, but after DAOC I can&#039;t figure out why I thought EQ was fun for so long.  It was neat when it was new but the end-game was extreemly boring.  DAOC was the opposite, the new content was okay, actually it was better than being a newbie in EQ but since I&#039;d already done the PvE thing in EQ I found it boring, however the end-game rocked.<br /><br />DAOC has gone through two mass exoduses of players, and neither were triggered by another game.  The first one they introduced an expansion called Trials of Atlantis.  ToA added a whole bunch of PvE that, even though they claimed wouldn&#039;t have an effect on RvR, made it so if you didn&#039;t do the new PvE content you were very gimped in RvR.  When I first started DAOC I refused help in any form because I wanted to make it on my own effort.  Even without power leveling or twinking or anything it took me about 3 times as long to get just the ToA stuff done so I could go RvR as all the PvE before ToA took me.  And I suposadly chose the hardest class to level.  I quit the game when ToA came out along with most of the other RvR people, but since we couldn&#039;t find anything else out there worth playing most of us went back, suffered through PvE for a few months, and started having fun again.<br /><br />Second mass exodus is still going on right now.  DAOC did a massive change in the PvP area, actually they literally replaced it.  Most of the people that used to PvP all the time have quit, for whatever reason (and there&#039;s alot of theories on exactly what that reason is and what will happen in the future) the game stopped being fun with the new changes.  However since most of their players were PvE people anyway who seem to like the new changes they haven&#039;t lost a large portion of their overall player base.  This time it&#039;s a little different for the players that quit - even though there&#039;s nothing else worth playing out there it&#039;s not a matter of returning to the game, getting the PvE out of the way, and having fun again.  This time the part of the game that was fun is gone and there is no reason to return, so I don&#039;t think they&#039;ll be getting their customers back.<br /><br />I think most of the people that quit a game when a new one comes out have been sick of it for a long time.  The new game means they finally have something else to do.  It&#039;s an oppurtinity to finally do what they&#039;ve been wanting to for a long time, not the real reason for the action.<br /><br />Since EQ has been out for a long time now, and every expansion has been new content in the form of more PvE catering to the &quot;ubers,&quot; I think anyone who doesn&#039;t like the type of game where all you do is work on your character would have left by now.  The people quitting in the future will do so because they have other things to do in life than sit at a computer for 40 hours a week (get a &quot;life,&quot;) or suddenly realize that they aren&#039;t having fun anymore, and that they really haven&#039;t been having fun for a long time.  It won&#039;t have anything to do with a new game.<br /><br />- Eric<br /><br />Used to play Hallertau but quit back in November of 2002 and sold the account.  Quit DAOC recently and am unable to find anything else worth playing.  Real life paintball is alot more fun than any computer game ever was, but I can&#039;t play that every night of the week.<br />
						</td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<td valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
								<td align="left" colspan="2" class="smalltext">
								</td>
							</tr><tr>
								<td align="left" valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
									&#171; <i>Last Edit: August 26, 2004, 01:03:19 pm by Khaevil</i> &#187;
								</td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
									<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/ip.gif" alt="" border="0" /> Logged
								</td>
							</tr></table>
						</td>
					</tr>
				</table>
			</td></tr>
		</table>
	</td></tr>
	<tr><td style="padding: 1px 1px 0 1px;">
		<a name="msg10487"></a>
		<table cellpadding="3" cellspacing="0" border="0" width="100%">
			<tr><td class="windowbg2">
				<table width="100%" cellpadding="5" cellspacing="0">
					<tr>
						<td valign="top" width="15%" rowspan="2">
							<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?action=profile;u=272" title="View the profile of Rednight">Rednight</a></b><br />
							<span class="smalltext">
								Hill Giant<br />
								<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/star.gif" alt="*" border="0" /><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/star.gif" alt="*" border="0" /><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/star.gif" alt="*" border="0" /><br />
								Gender: <img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/Male.gif" alt="Male" border="0" /><br />
								Posts: 141<br />
								<br />
								<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/YaBBImages/avatars/genjuro.gif" alt="" border="0" /><br />
								Huuh...Whaat...YEAAAH~!<br />
								<br />
								
								<a href="http://members.msn.com/mi_2_az@hotmail.com" target="_blank"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/msntalk.gif" alt="mi_2_az@hotmail.com" border="0" /></a>
								
								<br />
