	<tr><td style="padding: 1px 1px 0 1px;">
		<a name="msg10856"></a>
		<table cellpadding="3" cellspacing="0" border="0" width="100%">
			<tr><td class="windowbg2">
				<table width="100%" cellpadding="5" cellspacing="0">
					<tr>
						<td valign="top" width="15%" rowspan="2">
							<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?action=profile;u=835" title="View the profile of Keyes">Keyes</a></b><br />
							<span class="smalltext">
								Orc Pawn<br />
								<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/star.gif" alt="*" border="0" /><br />
								Posts: 4<br />
								<br />
								<br />
								
								
								
								<br />
								<a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?action=profile;u=835"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/icons/profile_sm.gif" alt="View Profile" title="View Profile" border="0" /></a>
							</span>
						</td>
						<td valign="top" width="85%" height="100%">
							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
								<td align="left" valign="middle"><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=1016.msg10856#msg10856"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/post/xx.gif" alt="" border="0" /></a></td>
								<td align="left" valign="middle">
									<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=1016.msg10856#msg10856">Re: Future of EQ</a></b><br />
									<span class="smalltext">&#171; <b>Reply #35 on:</b> September 06, 2004, 01:52:03 am &#187;</span></td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" height="20" nowrap="nowrap" style="font-size: smaller;">
								</td>
							</tr></table>
							<hr width="100%" size="1" class="hrcolor" />
							Well, my 2 cp on the future of EQ is that it will survive if SOE will listen to its&#039; player base.&nbsp; They seem to have started listening with the guild summit thing.<br /><br />I remember the early fascination with the game having started my first character in early May of 1999.&nbsp; After a few deletions and adjusting the stat points I settled on a character. <br /><br />There weren&#039;t any players I knew personally on Rodcet so I talked to people I knew who played electronic games and tired to convince them to play.&nbsp; I found one and he and I played together for about 6 months then he quit because he was frustrated with the difficulty in moving from zone to zone and traveling to the distant areas of Norrath.<br /><br />After he left I went looking for some players in the game who played at the same time I did and were close to my level.&nbsp; We formed a close bound and are still online friends. <br /><br />Some players joined guilds and progressed at a faster pace than those who chose unguilded.&nbsp; It was fun learning to cope with your classes abilities and weaknesses.&nbsp; I remember the first few Naggy and Vox raids when people were trying to find their corpses.&nbsp; Being a bard with corpse locate,&nbsp; I was asked to help and soon found out the bonuses of being in a guild.<br /><br />The early days I saw not only competition but also co-operation among guilds.&nbsp; The night when Vox was finally killed I believe everyone on the server was delighted.&nbsp; I can&#039;t say the same today when a new guild gets into Elementals or Time.<br /><br />The competition among guilds has been a boon and a bane.&nbsp; I would like to see a return to more co-operative sytem by having zones or trial events only available to 32 players of one class where the reward is something for the entire raid.<br /><br />EQ will always have my first attention when it comes to online games.&nbsp; I hope to be able play and make friends for years to come as long as they don&#039;t screw it up too bad with by alienating its player base.<br /><br />Keyes Sarabande
						</td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<td valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
								<td align="left" colspan="2" class="smalltext">
								</td>
							</tr><tr>
								<td align="left" valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
								</td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
									<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/ip.gif" alt="" border="0" /> Logged
								</td>
							</tr></table>
						</td>
					</tr>
				</table>
			</td></tr>
		</table>
	</td></tr>
	<tr><td style="padding: 1px 1px 0 1px;">
